ting `VoidScreen`, I\u2019ll add state variables using hooks. I can define a record type for the seek preview, maybe something like `typedef SeekPreview = ({int targetMs, int durationMs, double fraction});`. I need to make sure the state is properly set up and non-nullable as well. It's a bit intricate, but I think I can manage it!\n\n**Implementing callbacks in buildHeroGestureSurface**\n\nIn the `buildHeroGestureSurface`, I need to pass some callbacks. Specifically, I\u2019ll set `showSeekHud` to false if the platform is Linux. The `onSeekPreview` callback will update `seekPreview.value` with target, duration, and fraction, while `onSeekPreviewEnd` will set it to null. To detect if the platform is Linux, I can use `Theme.of(context).platform`. I\u2019ll define a boolean at the top of the build, and since `buildHeroGestureSurface` is nested within the build function, it should have access to the theme\u2019s palette effectively. It\u2019s a bit of a puzzle, but I\u2019m figuring it out!\n\n**Setting up crumb updates**\n\nI\u2019m planning to add a variable at the top to check if the platform is Linux: `final isLinux = Theme.of(context).platform == TargetPlatform.linux;`. I might also have a `final showSeekPreviewInCrumb = isLinux;` for clarity. \n\nNext, I'll update the `buildCrumb` function to show seek information when `seekPreview.value` isn\u2019t null and we're on Linux. The current crumb uses a Selector for path and leap glyph. Instead, I\u2019ll adjust the builder to display the target, duration, and progress. I think hiding the jump glyph and using a placeholder is the simplest approach here!\n\n**Formatting seek display**\n\nI\u2019m considering using mono typography for the seek label based on `crumbSize`. I think it might be unnecessary to show the jump glyph, so I\u2019ll decide to hide it for now. The progress label should definitely display as `${(fraction*100).round()}%`, ensuring it accurately reflects the fraction. \n\nThe full label might be formatted as `'${formatClock(targetMs)} / ${formatClock(durationMs)} \u2022 ${(fraction*100).round()}%'`. I\u2019ll want to make sure I'm using the right mono helper defined in `void_screen.dart` and check if I need to adjust any imports as well. It\u2019s a bit of a search, but I\u2019m getting there!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_03468175aa18e99e016a884fe7edc48197a1e3b45c887cd6eb\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqiFAUOQIrXjqZtfgXEvvgXDzAVLixR2syC-ZbLSj4HmVYFsK2lnCaW2w_kAEFxDpVYC8KBAMrneKTMW1My0YhrVvemQjf1wIvKJooYVVvgjuOBLnMMoVVQfsxJwdL7gBYXfx_ajnhbGir5Fk5oWSOyuakVW-F6u6sgkTPi2LdOWr9g-rfd5-QiuX9O0HNsjh1SBe41ht9Fj6B0IOIRSEPPGGpBkMyqOyZgzr2jTieTCrqB5Xhx8wQLIPIEd2rV_1edsfo-PO6LBgoEiWIznFDOaqMYIvGpmNSsCh_bxcj19Lhtc0icHjeuo7CxH06UhLIjFgKxcy8_dIKD2zz1zR67NnL_1dwSyMvp9kzD88uguEWK3tx32LRTEhbnwPbtwx190s0YwNrg8ZFK3vNCjKzoXjQU4Csbv0STwUmH3XuCSu75l8AMGGWoSqTtqJxNXEEboUdndmxKm-hESMohIhS8OklJbC8TujoiG9MMIzb4R2zd8Pc0HWi1j9WcO3ZFL69JgQU8T1xMAB_3H_6JgEWoqptdF7DqmYbUqjuYJFXt77F23mFPicMUe_e6EuIz_AKshRLYzWKis5eRpIO7lUvAcXS4xCvLg0ye4n_0WtaK22ZYJJvL0tmg0ALYWl6dStWex-97hVf_hJBZbbraGAU8BVK54DD4n1JZVBpWho3QC9kkuEfsaplQ482gBD9Y4ozROPnbbDSl-WODqEgdnJr_QLfHsawtfuhQlOfyqOzpCdvbz-oLAEQUbsS5hUqeUkrWiwqOCjK-r6ym1rwDSxhuYeDwcQXQgCZbhpGAKcHG376rHYfP3E0AmSDm7uXu08tYLSLdolQ8SwlmnFVJxCEEaLhbBR2HjuAPWQ1kEokr2KNOkubB4rIF16u12cuEJWhKGFuh8-BayAGN2Bc41_6Lrhqq92PuFdc6LL8PGUAAib8748Wx4hJ4DG8m9uSMU94Fs_K8lp_84fMHwCEPK3NDS2WUAQBWPs4ouhWj664qVAeLcyFFM0v0iukzw3mx32HNxHXUUtPwyY4mZ-eurOZktupHjTP6tXMc59o4Nj4w2lDjX1YG-JZm1c1p_H-chktI-Zbyz9RB-Kf9aCbDhaTKi-8pM0pm8GJRfta4k0jxOr4aG2mvJDjqd1l2WYG9phiofywSoPUcWyta5F-tChhaJpYYN41gT5mmGH5BVlbgCiwn1e2-RCje6GzCx_1Ddo3XjjYhr_Ei8qoVUbucMLkp5QlVIOpYPrg50oSyACNwZVtRQKgidfBXEIVPqAiMLg5XUJSeIM41iVJpasVAugl763A0U2Cb1QTHKV6DvqnlIgF7ql4ywPEnIX2cLU3i3o-n8QhKRCG3jxe4kZMC4ad4G5aIg_6VFxxltQQSDuKM4K7d99n_hiulFAGY-WY4n18bvgTJDb0qq10joURt8reF6zey9auAaJ3OSb1n8iqTWB7mn29Tti77gElH9ruloLfqfou3dBRi_Rb88jF3n6fHJMbtJY2UrV-DuhV-NJ5vfCMEnXO5mmZFDwf0XMYnYFUPbNOt_6